{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NEoj84pLThLYCDpjXC9i2Y","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Must-run for paper submission ===\n3\t\n4\t  - id: exp-001\n5\t    claim: 1\n6\t    description: \"Cross-architecture hidden-state extraction + layer sweep + static probe evaluation on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Includes mandatory layer sweep (all layers) to find best layer for 64-layer models before probe evaluation. Validates Claim 1 generalizes beyond r1-8b.\"\n7\t    priority: P0\n8\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n9\t    deps: []\n10\t    models: [DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B, QwQ-32B]\n11\t    notes: \"32B models have 64 layers, 5120-d hidden. r1-8b best layer was 14/32 (44% depth) → expect best around layer 28-32 for 64-layer models. Extract ALL layers for sweep, then select best for subsequent experiments. Must do layer sweep BEFORE reporting static probe results — using wrong layer would produce false negative.\"\n12\t\n13\t  - id: exp-002\n14\t    claim: 2\n15\t    description: \"Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation: temporal LR W=15 on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Validate +30pp coverage improvement holds cross-architecture.\"\n16\t    priority: P0\n17\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n18\t    deps: [exp-001]\n19\t    models: [DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B, QwQ-32B]\n20\t\n21\t  - id: exp-003\n22\t    claim: [1, 2]\n23\t    description: \"Cross-model transfer: train probe on r1-8b (Llama), test on r1-32b/QwQ (Qwen2.5). Train on Qwen, test on Llama. Measures zero-shot cross-architecture generalization.\"\n24\t    priority: P0\n25\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n26\t    deps: [exp-001]\n27\t    notes: \"Key for cross-architecture story. Projection head needed (4096→5120 or vice versa).\"\n28\t\n29\t  - id: exp-004\n30\t    claim: 3\n31\t    description: \"Lead time analysis across models: confirm negative lead time finding on 32B models. Report lead time distribution per model.\"\n32\t    priority: P0\n33\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n34\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n35\t\n36\t  - id: exp-005\n37\t    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n38\t    description: \"TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis baseline: implement and evaluate on all 3 models. Expected to fail (signal in minor PCs, Fisher drops 17→1 in PCA-3D).\"\n39\t    priority: P0\n40\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n41\t    deps: [exp-001]\n42\t    notes: \"Critical baseline for 'existing detectors fail' claim. Use safe traces to estimate covariance, compute MD per step.\"\n43\t\n44\t  - id: exp-006\n45\t    claim: [1, 2]\n46\t    description: \"Bootstrap confidence intervals + threshold-independent metrics: 1000 bootstrap resamples on all key metrics (coverage, lead time, accuracy). ALSO report AUROC, precision-recall curves, detection delay CDF, cross-validation per-fold variance, and FPR on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5).\"\n47\t    priority: P0\n48\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n49\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002, exp-003, exp-004, exp-005]\n50\t\n51\t  # === P1: Important but deferrable ===\n52\t\n53\t  - id: exp-007\n54\t    claim: 2\n55\t    description: \"Window size ablation: W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25 on all 3 models. Find optimal W and show diminishing returns curve.\"\n56\t    priority: P1\n57\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n58\t    deps: [exp-001]\n59\t\n60\t  - id: exp-008\n61\t    claim: 2\n62\t    description: \"Layer selection ablation: all layers (not just 14) for temporal probe on 32B models. Confirm middle-layer finding generalizes.\"\n63\t    priority: P1\n64\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n65\t    deps: [exp-001]\n66\t\n67\t  - id: exp-009\n68\t    claim: 2\n69\t    description: \"16-label taxonomy supervision: use fine-grained labels (Type 1/2/3/4) instead of binary commitment for richer training signal. May improve both coverage and timing.\"\n70\t    priority: P1\n71\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n72\t    deps: [exp-001]\n73\t    notes: \"Addresses reviewer concern about underusing available supervision.\"\n74\t\n75\t  - id: exp-010\n76\t    claim: 3\n77\t    description: \"Oracle decomposition: why can oracle but not probes achieve positive lead time? Analyze what label patterns encode that hidden states don't.\"\n78\t    priority: P1\n79\t    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n80\t    deps: [exp-004]\n81\t    notes: \"For Discussion section. May reveal what architectural changes could close the gap.\"\n82\t\n83\t  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n84\t\n85\t  - id: exp-011\n86\t    claim: 2\n87\t    description: \"OpenThinker-7B (Qwen2.5-7B base): 4th model for 2×2 architecture×scale matrix. Controls for scale confound.\"\n88\t    priority: P2\n89\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n90\t    deps: [exp-002]\n91\t    notes: \"From Human Review Note point 5. Adds Qwen2.5-7B to complement Llama-8B for scale-matched comparison.\"\n92\t\n93\t  - id: exp-012\n94\t    claim: [1, 2]\n95\t    description: \"GRU/Attention probe as upper bound: verify GRU finding holds on 32B models with more data. If still no improvement over LR, strengthens 'simplicity is optimal' story.\"\n96\t    priority: P2\n97\t    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n98\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n99\t\n100\t  - id: exp-013\n101\t    claim: [1, 2]\n102\t    description: \"Text-based baseline: sentence-BERT embeddings (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) + same temporal window LR (W=15) on CoT text. Compare coverage/lead time to hidden-state probes. CRITICAL for proving hidden-state monitoring adds unique value over cheap text monitoring. If text achieves comparable performance, paper motivation needs restructuring.\"\n103\t    priority: P0\n104\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0.5\n105\t    deps: []\n106\t    notes: \"No GPU needed for embedding extraction (small model, CPU-feasible). Run on all 4 models. This is the single most important missing baseline per Dream review (flagged by all 3 tiers, both reviewers).\"\n107\t\n108\t  - id: exp-014\n109\t    claim: 3\n110\t    description: \"Bayesian Online Change-Point Detection (BOCPD) on per-step probe scores: apply Adams & MacKay 2007 to the sequence of probe confidence scores. Could achieve positive lead time by detecting distributional shift before textual commitment. Also test CUSUM as simpler alternative.\"\n111\t    priority: P0\n112\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0.5\n113\t    deps: [exp-001]\n114\t    notes: \"Addresses both 'no method novelty' and 'no positive lead time' criticisms simultaneously. If BOCPD achieves reliable lead time where GRU doesn't, this becomes a genuine methods contribution. If it also fails, strengthens the 'fundamental limitation' narrative.\"\n115\t\n116\t  - id: exp-015\n117\t    claim: [1, 2]\n118\t    description: \"False positive analysis: run all probes (static, temporal, GRU, BOCPD) on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5). Report FPR, precision-recall curves at various thresholds. Essential for deployment utility claims.\"\n119\t    priority: P0\n120\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0.5\n121\t    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n122\t    notes: \"Dream flagged missing FPR as critical gap across median and worst tiers. Without this, 'coverage' metric is uninterpretable — a probe that fires everywhere gets 100% coverage.\"\n123\t\n124\tgpu_budget_total: \"~37 A100-hours (P0: 19.5h, P1: 8h, P2: 8h, new P0: +1.5h)\"\n125\ttimeline: \"P0 experiments: May 17-19 (3 days). P1: May 19-21. Paper writing: May 21-25. Text baseline (exp-013) can start immediately (no GPU). BOCPD (exp-014) after first probe scores available.\"\n126\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d66c63b-15da-4009-ae0c-c9250a6c1577","uuid":"0e32d7cd-d7af-4c41-a2d2-0732371c5d04","timestamp":"2026-05-22T09:01:02.201Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_5/projects/contrastive_trace_safety/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n  # === P0: Must-run for paper submission ===\n\n  - id: exp-001\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"Cross-architecture hidden-state extraction + layer sweep + static probe evaluation on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Includes mandatory layer sweep (all layers) to find best layer for 64-layer models before probe evaluation. Validates Claim 1 generalizes beyond r1-8b.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n    deps: []\n    models: [DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B, QwQ-32B]\n    notes: \"32B models have 64 layers, 5120-d hidden. r1-8b best layer was 14/32 (44% depth) → expect best around layer 28-32 for 64-layer models. Extract ALL layers for sweep, then select best for subsequent experiments. Must do layer sweep BEFORE reporting static probe results — using wrong layer would produce false negative.\"\n\n  - id: exp-002\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"Cross-architecture temporal window evaluation: temporal LR W=15 on r1-32b and QwQ-32B. Validate +30pp coverage improvement holds cross-architecture.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    models: [DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-32B, QwQ-32B]\n\n  - id: exp-003\n    claim: [1, 2]\n    description: \"Cross-model transfer: train probe on r1-8b (Llama), test on r1-32b/QwQ (Qwen2.5). Train on Qwen, test on Llama. Measures zero-shot cross-architecture generalization.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    notes: \"Key for cross-architecture story. Projection head needed (4096→5120 or vice versa).\"\n\n  - id: exp-004\n    claim: 3\n    description: \"Lead time analysis across models: confirm negative lead time finding on 32B models. Report lead time distribution per model.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n\n  - id: exp-005\n    claim: [1, 2, 3]\n    description: \"TrajGuard-style Mahalanobis baseline: implement and evaluate on all 3 models. Expected to fail (signal in minor PCs, Fisher drops 17→1 in PCA-3D).\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    notes: \"Critical baseline for 'existing detectors fail' claim. Use safe traces to estimate covariance, compute MD per step.\"\n\n  - id: exp-006\n    claim: [1, 2]\n    description: \"Bootstrap confidence intervals + threshold-independent metrics: 1000 bootstrap resamples on all key metrics (coverage, lead time, accuracy). ALSO report AUROC, precision-recall curves, detection delay CDF, cross-validation per-fold variance, and FPR on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5).\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n    deps: [exp-001, exp-002, exp-003, exp-004, exp-005]\n\n  # === P1: Important but deferrable ===\n\n  - id: exp-007\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"Window size ablation: W=1,3,5,10,15,20,25 on all 3 models. Find optimal W and show diminishing returns curve.\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [exp-001]\n\n  - id: exp-008\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"Layer selection ablation: all layers (not just 14) for temporal probe on 32B models. Confirm middle-layer finding generalizes.\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n    deps: [exp-001]\n\n  - id: exp-009\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"16-label taxonomy supervision: use fine-grained labels (Type 1/2/3/4) instead of binary commitment for richer training signal. May improve both coverage and timing.\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    notes: \"Addresses reviewer concern about underusing available supervision.\"\n\n  - id: exp-010\n    claim: 3\n    description: \"Oracle decomposition: why can oracle but not probes achieve positive lead time? Analyze what label patterns encode that hidden states don't.\"\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 1\n    deps: [exp-004]\n    notes: \"For Discussion section. May reveal what architectural changes could close the gap.\"\n\n  # === P2: Nice-to-have ===\n\n  - id: exp-011\n    claim: 2\n    description: \"OpenThinker-7B (Qwen2.5-7B base): 4th model for 2×2 architecture×scale matrix. Controls for scale confound.\"\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n    deps: [exp-002]\n    notes: \"From Human Review Note point 5. Adds Qwen2.5-7B to complement Llama-8B for scale-matched comparison.\"\n\n  - id: exp-012\n    claim: [1, 2]\n    description: \"GRU/Attention probe as upper bound: verify GRU finding holds on 32B models with more data. If still no improvement over LR, strengthens 'simplicity is optimal' story.\"\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 4\n    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n\n  - id: exp-013\n    claim: [1, 2]\n    description: \"Text-based baseline: sentence-BERT embeddings (all-MiniLM-L6-v2) + same temporal window LR (W=15) on CoT text. Compare coverage/lead time to hidden-state probes. CRITICAL for proving hidden-state monitoring adds unique value over cheap text monitoring. If text achieves comparable performance, paper motivation needs restructuring.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0.5\n    deps: []\n    notes: \"No GPU needed for embedding extraction (small model, CPU-feasible). Run on all 4 models. This is the single most important missing baseline per Dream review (flagged by all 3 tiers, both reviewers).\"\n\n  - id: exp-014\n    claim: 3\n    description: \"Bayesian Online Change-Point Detection (BOCPD) on per-step probe scores: apply Adams & MacKay 2007 to the sequence of probe confidence scores. Could achieve positive lead time by detecting distributional shift before textual commitment. Also test CUSUM as simpler alternative.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0.5\n    deps: [exp-001]\n    notes: \"Addresses both 'no method novelty' and 'no positive lead time' criticisms simultaneously. If BOCPD achieves reliable lead time where GRU doesn't, this becomes a genuine methods contribution. If it also fails, strengthens the 'fundamental limitation' narrative.\"\n\n  - id: exp-015\n    claim: [1, 2]\n    description: \"False positive analysis: run all probes (static, temporal, GRU, BOCPD) on safe traces (final_judgment=0.5). Report FPR, precision-recall curves at various thresholds. Essential for deployment utility claims.\"\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0.5\n    deps: [exp-001, exp-002]\n    notes: \"Dream flagged missing FPR as critical gap across median and worst tiers. Without this, 'coverage' metric is uninterpretable — a probe that fires everywhere gets 100% coverage.\"\n\ngpu_budget_total: \"~37 A100-hours (P0: 19.5h, P1: 8h, P2: 8h, new P0: +1.5h)\"\ntimeline: \"P0 experiments: May 17-19 (3 days). P1: May 19-21. Paper writing: May 21-25. Text baseline (exp-013) can start immediately (no GPU). BOCPD (exp-014) after first probe scores available.\"\n","numLines":126,"startLine":1,"totalLines":126}}}
